    id 46
    label "W-UEGcogulU"
    step 0
    date "2016-10-05T15:47:38Z"
    title "Nanotechnology for Clean Water"
    description "In a &amp;#8220;Science Nation&amp;#8221; video released by the National Science Foundation, Stony Brook chemist Benjamin Hsiao explains that traditional water filters are made of polymer membranes with tiny pores to filter out bacteria and viruses. Hsiao&amp;#8217;s filters are made of fibers that are all tangled up, and the pores are the natural gaps between the strands. The team&amp;#8217;s first success at making the new nanofilters uses a technique called electrospinning to produce nanofibers under an electrical field."
