    id 110
    label "mRQTM0xU9r0"
    step 0
    date "2021-04-28T13:30:05Z"
    title "Nanotechnology - The Future Technology | Nanochemistry | Nanoscience"
    description "This video gives you an introduction to Nanochemistry, a combination of Nanoscience and Nanotechnology.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;00:00 Introduction to Nanochemistry&amp;#10;00:35 Invention of Nanotechnology&amp;#10;01:00 Molecular Nanotechnology&amp;#10;01:22 Machines can be manufactured at Nanoscale&amp;#10;01:45 Scanning Tunnel Microscope&amp;#10;02:25 Quantum Tunneling&amp;#10;02:50 Conclusion&amp;#10;&amp;#10;In 1959, an American physicist, Richard Feynman came up with the concept &amp;#34;There is plenty of space at the bottom&amp;#8221;, in which, he believed that technology and machines can be manufactured at nanoscale.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;In 2017 can you imagine that we are able to manufacture transistors at the size of 7 nanometers? Which is 200 times smaller than the HIV virus and 500 times smaller than your red blood cell.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Scientists believe, when a transistor is smaller than 7nm, it exhibits a property called Quantum Tunneling.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Now we will dive into Nanochemistry.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Subscribe to our channel for more videos. Press the bell icon for personalized notifications to our videos.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The Voice of Aftertutor:&amp;#10;NaturalReaders: https://www.naturalreaders.com/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The music of the video here: &amp;#10;Audioblocks: https://www.audioblocks.com/"
