  [
    id 169
    label "iME0NtUNIEI"
    step 0
    date "2020-07-02T12:01:30Z"
    title "Nanotechnology(Engineering on atomic scales!) l  l"
    description "Simple explanation about nanotechnology in Tamil (&amp;#2980;&amp;#2990;&amp;#3007;&amp;#2996;&amp;#3021;)&amp;#10;What is Nanotechnology  and How much impact will it have on various industries? &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Nanotechnology is a fascinating field&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Although modern nanoscience and nanotechnology are quite new, nanoscale materials were used for centuries. Alternate-sized gold and silver particles created colors in the stained glass windows of medieval churches hundreds of years ago. The artists back then just didn&amp;#8217;t know that the process they used to create these beautiful works of art actually led to changes in the composition of the materials they were working with.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Nanoscience and nanotechnology involve the ability to see and to control individual atoms and molecules. Everything on Earth is made up of atoms&amp;#8212;the food we eat, the clothes we wear, the buildings and houses we live in, and our own bodies.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;But something as small as an atom is impossible to see with the naked eye. In fact, it&amp;#8217;s impossible to see with the microscopes typically used in a high school science classes. The microscopes needed to see things at the nanoscale were invented relatively recently&amp;#8212;about 30 years ago.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The ideas and concepts behind nanoscience and nanotechnology started with a talk entitled &amp;#8220;There&amp;#8217;s Plenty of Room at the Bottom&amp;#8221; by physicist Richard Feynman at an American Physical Society meeting at the California Institute of Technology (CalTech) on December 29, 1959, long before the term nanotechnology was used. In his talk, Feynman described a process in which scientists would be able to manipulate and control individual atoms and molecules&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Once scientists had the right tools, such as the scanning tunneling microscope (STM) and the atomic force microscope (AFM), the age of nanotechnology was born.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Today's scientists and engineers are finding a wide variety of ways to deliberately make materials at the nanoscale to take advantage of their enhanced properties such as higher strength, lighter weight, increased control of light spectrum, and greater chemical reactivity than their larger-scale counterparts.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Thank you for watching this video : nanotechnology in tamil&amp;#10;Like, &amp;#10;Sources:&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://simple.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanotechnology&amp;#10;https://www.explainthatstuff.com/nanotechnologyforkids.html&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.dummies.com/education/science/nanotechnology/what-is-nanotechnology/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nano.gov/nanotech-101/what/definition&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nano.gov/nanotech-101/special&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.dummies.com/education/science/nanotechnology/how-materials-change-in-nanoscale/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://teachers.yale.edu/curriculum/viewer/initiative_10.05.06_u&amp;#10; https://www.sciencelearn.org.nz/resources/1676-novel-properties-emerge-at-the-nanoscale&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://ec.europa.eu/health/scien_committees/opinions_layman/nanomaterials/en/l-2/1.htm&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nanowerk.com/how_nanoparticles_are_made.php&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nanowerk.com/what_is_graphene.php&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/materials-science/carbon-nanotubes&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nanowerk.com/nanotechnology/introduction/introduction_to_nanotechnology_22.php&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.nano.gov/you/nanotechnology-benefits&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.understandingnano.com/medicine.html&amp;#10;&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.understandingnano.com/nanotech-applications.html&amp;#10;&amp;#10; https://www.azonano.com/amp/article.aspx?ArticleID=4840&amp;#10;&amp;#10; https://www.researchgate.net/publication/281730052_Gene_Therapy_Potential_applications_of_nanotechnology&amp;#10;&amp;#10; https://disruptionhub.com/6-applications-of-nanotechnology/&amp;#10; https://www.nanowerk.com/spotlight/spotid=1781.php&amp;#10;&amp;#10; https://www.nanowerk.com/spotlight/spotid=30804.php&amp;#10;&amp;#10;-----------------------------------------------------------------------&amp;#10; &amp;#10;More Interesting Videos to watch&amp;#128521;:&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpgRRjgKvBJk1pPDB8JejgcL_0lAi13DH&amp;#38;feature=share&amp;#10;-----------------------------------------------------------------------&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Future Science &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Welcome to Future Science&amp;#10; Quality content on Science and Technology through appealing visuals. &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Future Science aims to be a trusted and reliable channel. Therefore, information is checked various times, gathered from reliable sources and links to all sources are provided in the description.&amp;#10; Learning new things is always fun and exciting. Join us on a wonderful journey of discovery and learning. &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Subscribe now and join the community &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Instagram Handle :&amp;#10;&amp;#10;https://instagram.com/futuresciencee?igshid=od9j2uop8aoi------------------------------------&amp;#10;Music Credits:&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Lights by Sappheiros https://soundcloud.com/sappheirosmusic &amp;#10;Creative Commons &amp;#8212; Attribution 3.0 Unported &amp;#8212; CC BY 3.0 &amp;#10;Free Download / Stream: https://bit.ly/LightsSappheiros &amp;#10;Music promoted by Audio Library https://youtu.be/-lbbHQbZNKg&amp;#10;----------------------------------------&amp;#10;Track: Fusion &amp;#8212; KV [Audio Library Release]&amp;#10;Music provided by Audio Library Plus&amp;#10;Watch: https://youtu.be/gp613GReEo4&amp;#10;Free Download / Stream: https://alplus.io/fusion&amp;#10;----------------------------------------"
    channeltitle "Future Science"
